# baseline.config — PROVISIONAL control profile
#
# Profile:        baseline (control / reproduction / performance comparison)
# Kbase:          r54p0-01eac0 (primary)  [+ patches/virtual-device/ 0001-0006]
# Kernel:         UNKNOWN — not selected. ARM GUIDANCE: latest Android Common
#                 Kernel, or latest Linux stable/LTS (see research/program-scope.md §4)
# Patch set:      vendor/virtual-device 0001-0006 (VERIFIED to apply to r54p0)
# Scope class:    INVESTIGATION/DISCOVERY-ONLY as an x86 virtual environment
#                 (DECISION-1, research/program-scope.md §8.5) because it needs
#                 MALI_PLATFORM_NAME="vexpress" + a GPU target, which are outside
#                 the Kbase build allowlist (§8.3). It is deliberately
#                 uninstrumented and defines the INTENDED conforming config shape
#                 for real hardware. No x86 NO_MALI build is a validation env.
# Generated from: Arm's virtual-platform guide Kbase options (verbatim) + a
#                 kernel baseline that does not exist yet. NOT a savedefconfig.
# Validation:     PROVISIONAL — never fed to a build. Full config UNKNOWN.
# Config hash:    N/A (placeholder fragment; no real .config has been produced)
#
# NOT a valid .config. NOT the output of make defconfig/savedefconfig.
# This fragment does not yet exist against any kernel, so it contains only
# (a) Kbase options verified from Arm's supplied PDF, and (b) placeholders.
#
# Purpose of this profile: control / reproduction / performance comparison.
# It should be the CLOSEST to the Arm/default configuration. It carries NO
# instrumentation (no KCOV, no KASAN, no DEBUG_KERNEL) so it can serve as the
# uninstrumented reference against which the other profiles are compared.
#
# Conforming-by-design: to remain IN SCOPE, every delta this profile introduces
# relative to the eventual defconfig baseline must be either a NO-OP or
# ALLOWLISTED per research/program-scope.md §5. The mandatory savedefconfig-diff
# check (project spec §18) must confirm this before the profile is called
# conforming.

# --- Kbase driver options, verbatim from Arm's virtual-platform guide ------
CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=m
CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MALI_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG=n
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI=y
# CONFIG_MALI_REAL_HW is not set
# GPU target = the LATEST target defined by r54p0 (DECISION-2, findings.md F-4),
# not the guide's older "tKRx" (arch 13). tDRx = arch 14.8.5. Investigation-only.
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI_DEFAULT_GPU="tDRx"
CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME="vexpress"

# --- Kernel hard build gates, set explicitly ------------------------------
# VERIFIED: midgard/Kbuild raises $(error ...) for FIVE unconditional symbols at
# lines 29,33,37,41,45. The test is `ifeq ($(CONFIG_X),n)`, which does NOT catch
# an unset (empty) symbol, so an unset value could pass silently. Set all five
# explicitly. These are almost certainly default y in a normal defconfig, so
# setting them is expected to be a NO-OP delta — to be CONFIRMED by the
# savedefconfig diff, not assumed. See findings.md F-3 and F-11.
#
# DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND (Kbuild:41-42) was MISSING from an earlier revision
# of these fragments; it is a hard gate like the other four.
# FW_LOADER (Kbuild:45-46) is additionally selected by MALI_MIDGARD, so it is
# satisfied automatically; it is listed for completeness.
#
# Two further gates are CONDITIONAL and only fire if their feature is enabled;
# neither is enabled by any profile here:
#   MALI_PRFCNT_SET_SELECT_VIA_DEBUG_FS -> requires CONFIG_DEBUG_FS   (Kbuild:49-51)
#   MALI_FENCE_DEBUG                    -> requires CONFIG_SYNC_FILE (Kbuild:55-57)
CONFIG_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y
CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ=y
CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y
CONFIG_DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND=y
CONFIG_FW_LOADER=y

# --- DELIBERATELY ABSENT (this is the control) -----------------------------
# CONFIG_KCOV, CONFIG_KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL  -> none; uninstrumented reference
# CONFIG_KASAN*, CONFIG_UBSAN*             -> none
# CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL, CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO   -> none
# CONFIG_MALI_KCOV                         -> not selectable in-tree anyway (F-2)

# --- UNRESOLVED, for the build phase --------------------------------------
# - Exact kernel version and its defconfig baseline.
# - Complete minimal x86_64 configuration (UNKNOWN until a build).
# - RESOLVED: GPU target is now "tDRx", the latest in r54p0 (findings.md F-4 /
#   DECISION-2). Whether it initialises in the NO_MALI path is NOT_TESTED.